      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/20/indian-man-sentenced-prison-murder-plot-sikh-separatist",
      "description": "<p>Nikhil Gupta admitted to plotting with Indian government official to hire hitman to murder dual US-Canadian citizen</p><p>An Indian ⁠man was sentenced to more ⁠than 19 ​years in US prison on Friday after admitting to orchestrating a failed Indian government-backed plot to kill a Sikh separatist in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york\">New York ⁠City</a>, in connection with what US and Canadian authorities have called a broader effort to target Indian dissidents.</p><p>Nikhil Gupta, 55, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/13/nikhil-gupta-assassination-plot-pleads-guilty\">pleaded guilty</a> in February to murder-for-hire, conspiracy ⁠to commit murder-for-hire and conspiracy to commit money laundering.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/20/indian-man-sentenced-prison-murder-plot-sikh-separatist\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
